### 4.3. Training Strategy Comparison

To explore the capability of GRPO on agentic training, we

compare GRPO against RFT-only and RFT+GRPO. As presented in Fig. 3, directly training with GRPO outperformes RFT-only and RFT+GRPO. Moreover, although RFT has accetable performance, the more steps RFT proceeds, the less improvement GRPO makes after the cold start. This conclusion contradicts with previous SWE agents trained with RL

(Ma et al., 2025), however, it aligns with the broader field of

reinforcement learning, where RFT and SFT (as a cold start) is effective only when the pretrained model is not strong enough (Guo et al., 2024a). When the pretrained model is strong enough and data is high-quality, directly training a model with RL is better than training after SFT (RFT) as its cold start.

